The page opens as a broadsheet masthead — *The Bill Gazette* — followed by a scrolling ticker, a drop-capped "lead bill," a clickable dotted-leader index, and the full 25-limerick ledger with marginalia, a slowly panning engraving plate on several entries, a self-drawing "Index of Bills" chart in the economist's card, Jurgen's telegram, a scattered-postcard engraving collage, and a working "compose your own Bill" form that types out a fresh limerick. All three keywords — *economist* (No. 23), *bill* (throughout), and *jurgen* (No. 24 and the colophon) — appear in the copy, and every animation honors `prefers-reduced-motion`.
